Z||000006||Mach10||12-05-2001||08:21 AM||||Well, personally, I don't believe it... Unless you've seen them injectors yourself... I'd be inclined to call  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> on your mechanic... The injectors are not a stressed part... One thing I want to know: Why on EARTH would someone dropping the fuel tank in the middle of the car go through the trouble of pulling the upper plenum apart?!? To check for "blown" injectors? Sounds like what we Canadians call a Snow-Job....<P>I've heard of plugged or blown injectors, but blown only in the sense that the coils had melted... Injectors don't usually explode unless you have some SERIOUS timing issues, and you're backfiring up the intake..||||reg||4
Z||000007||Fie Ro||12-06-2001||06:12 AM||||I havent seen the injectors myself so I have to rely (ahem!) on the mechanic. Maybe it's another bullshit story of them. <BR>But the story was: the fuelpump was bad, they replaced it, still couldn't get the engine to work, and at last they removed the plenum and found 3 cracked injectors and replaced them.<BR>Now I wish I had seen them.<BR>I will try to call them if they still can remember what really happened because I'm seriously thinking of taking the plenum off. Car isn't running for quite a while now, I hate that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
