Z||000013||Mach10||12-06-2001||10:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fie Ro:<BR><B>I havent seen the injectors myself so I have to rely (ahem!) on the mechanic. Maybe it's another bullshit story of them. <BR>But the story was: the fuelpump was bad, they replaced it, still couldn't get the engine to work, and at last they removed the plenum and found 3 cracked injectors and replaced them.<BR>Now I wish I had seen them.<BR>I will try to call them if they still can remember what really happened because I'm seriously thinking of taking the plenum off. Car isn't running for quite a while now, I hate that   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Ah... That sounds a little better. But they didn't consult you before tearing into it? Unless you know them really well (like I know one of my mechanics) they shouldn't EVER do that. <P>If they were cracked, it's possible that they were taken off wrong, forced in improperly at some point, or any other number of possibilities. But, (and a TB backfire aside) I could not see how they could break like that on their own  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||7
Z||000014||Fie Ro||12-13-2001||05:55 AM||||Well,<BR>I got the car to a garage and I decided to take the plenum of. At first sight the injectors and fuelrail seem ok but when I got the injectors off the rail there was a lot of rubbish inside them ! Lots of rusty particals......I brought them to a remanufacture shop and they said they will be able to clean them, however I think one or more are broken. They charge F70,- (about $ 25/30) per injector to clean.<P>I hope that helps.||||reg||4
